The **Recent Calls** panel gives you a quick, contextual view of the latest calls handled by the agent you're currently editing. It's designed to help you validate changes and debug behavior without switching away from the Advanced Editor.

<Info>
This panel shows calls from the **last 30 days**, up to a maximum of 20 calls, ordered by most recent first.
</Info>

## Where to find it

The Recent Calls panel lives in the right-side panel area of the Advanced Editor, alongside Copilot, Playground, Tests, and Version History.

<Steps>
  <Step title="Open an agent in the Advanced Editor">
    Select any agent from your Agents list and open it in the Advanced Editor.
  </Step>
  <Step title="Switch to the Recent Calls tab">
    In the right panel, click on the **Recent Calls** icon to load the latest activity for this specific agent.
  </Step>
  <Step title="Review call details">
    Each entry shows the call status, direction (from → to), a short summary, relative time, and duration.
  </Step>
</Steps>

## What you can do

- **Refresh**: Click the refresh icon to reload the list on demand.
- **Open a call**: Click any call entry to open its full details (recording, transcript, and evaluation) in a new tab.
- **View all calls**: Use the **View all** button to jump to the full Call History, pre-filtered by this agent.

<Tabs>
  <Tab title="Success indicator">
    Calls marked as successful display a green checkmark badge next to the status, based on your configured evaluation criteria.
  </Tab>
  <Tab title="Status badges">
    Each call shows a colored status badge (e.g. Finished, No answer, Busy, Ringing, Voicemail) so you can scan activity at a glance.
  </Tab>
</Tabs>

<Warning>
If no calls have occurred in the last 30 days, the panel will display an empty state. This does not mean the agent is broken — it simply hasn't received calls recently.
</Warning>